														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1698569">
									

<p>Some scientific background for the uninitiated:</p>
<p>The Permian-Triassic extinction event, known among some in the paleontological circle as the &quot;Great Dying&quot;, was the most devastating extinction event in Earth's history. Far more potent than the more famous Cretaceous-Paleogene event 65 million years ago, the Great Dying resulted in the extinction of approximately 90 to 96% of all species alive during that time, a catastrophe of such proportions that it took <em>ten million years</em> for the Earth to recover. And unlike the death of the dinosaurs, there's no convenient smoking gun to point at to suggest exactly what caused it; 252 million years wipes out pretty much any kind of evidence that we could go on.</p>
<p>All we know is that <em>something</em> was aware of what was going on and actively trying to save as much life as possible when it happened. Whether it was Mother Earth herself or an observant alien intelligence is unknown; for all we know this event was intentionally caused and the ark a mere afterthought.</p>

							</div>

								
					
